.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
#include \(dqserver.h\(dq

int protocol_parse_command(const char *line, char *cmd, char *arg, size_t argsize);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Parses a v1 protocol input line into a command verb and its argument.
The first whitespace\-delimited word is extracted, uppercased, and
stored in \f[CR]cmd\f[R].
The remainder of the line (after skipping whitespace) is copied to
\f[CR]arg\f[R] with trailing whitespace trimmed.
.PP
The command word is limited to 31 characters and is always converted to
uppercase using \f[CR]toupper(3)\f[R].
Leading and trailing whitespace on the entire line is handled
gracefully.
.PP
This function is the primary dispatcher for the v1 text protocol.
For v2 JSON message parsing, see \f[CR]json_get_string(3)\f[R].
