.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
The command verb is always uppercased, so \f[CR]\(dqauth\(dq\f[R],
\f[CR]\(dqAuth\(dq\f[R], and \f[CR]\(dqAUTH\(dq\f[R] all produce
\f[CR]\(dqAUTH\(dq\f[R] in \f[CR]cmd\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
The argument is copied verbatim (except for trailing whitespace
trimming).
No uppercasing or other transformation is applied to the argument.
.IP \(bu 2
If the command word exceeds 31 characters, it is silently truncated.
.IP \(bu 2
If the argument exceeds \f[CR]argsize \- 1\f[R] bytes, it is truncated
